{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fvfmy3anewzgwhoaf7dszetxz6s7myy6tbuu5iozpd7dkrgq76yq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — all four phases pass.** The C is an inlined `stb_ds.h` plus a `str_put` driver; the Rust translation is faithful.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | **16/16, diff empty**, 0 non-libc undefined in the Rust `.so` |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row | **67/67 rows** pass across randomized inputs (fixed-seed splitmix64) |\n| Binary stdout | No executable exists; the public driver `str_put`'s stdout compared **byte-for-byte** via `dup2` for ~1000 inputs incl. 5 seeded 200-call sequences |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row | **46/46 `[x]` rows** have a passing error-path test; 9 `[U]` rows proved dead code |\n| Every feature combination | `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; both `default` and `--no-default-features` verified by `run_verification.sh` |\n\n95 tests in 9 binaries, stable over 5 consecutive runs. Every call goes through `libloading` into both `.so`s — never a direct Rust call.\n\n## One real bug found and fixed\n\n`STBDS_ASSERT` is plain `assert` and the C is built **without `NDEBUG`** (the `.so` imports `__assert_fail`), but the Rust had **no assertions at all**. This is reachable through the public ABI: a non-tail `stbds_hmdel_key` on a `SH_STRDUP` map with `mode == 2` makes the relocation re-lookup hash the raw pointer bytes, `find_slot` returns `-1`, and C aborts at `STBDS_ASSERT(slot >= 0)` — while the Rust silently wrote `b->index[i]` **one bucket before `table->storage`** (heap corruption). Added all 8 C assertions to `src/lib.rs`; `tests/phase_c_aborts.rs` now runs the case in a child process per library and asserts both die with the same signal (SIGABRT/134).\n\n## Notable C quirks confirmed reproduced\n\n- `int` sign-extension in the SipHash byte loads (`d[3] << 24`) — swept with high-bit-forced bytes at every word offset.\n- `hash < 2 → hash += 2`: reached *on purpose* by exploiting `hash_string(\"\", seed) == K + seed` to pick a seed yielding raw hash 0 and 1.\n- `512 << (block>>1)` UB shift in `stbds_stralloc`: for `block` 110–127 it overflows to 0, for 128+ gcc's `shl` masks the count `& 63`. Rust matches bit-for-bit. (`block >= 46` is untestable — the C itself asks for ≥4 GiB and segfaults on the NULL.)\n- `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)` passing a struct by value into varargs.\n- `temp_key` not refreshed in the wrap-around scan loop; `(unsigned char)` truncation of out-of-range `shmode_func` modes (`256 → 0`, `-1 → 255`) selecting the `switch` arm.\n\nThree harness artifacts were fixed rather than \"fixed\" in the Rust: uninitialized element value-bytes, uninitialized `table->temp_key`, and cross-test interference from the per-library global `stbds_hash_seed` (tests are now serialized by a mutex and reseed both libraries)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":284384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":575,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8aadc4a-4ab4-435a-be5e-d5e51011374e","uuid":"34ed3b4b-b6fb-492d-a8cd-a96abb3fbdd6","timestamp":"2026-09-05T12:38:42.057Z"}
